# Site mode and llms.txt

This documentation is a workbook. The sidebar, the routed URLs, the deep links you
can reload — none of it is hand-written front-end code. It's **site mode**: the
runtime reading an [`app`](/serving/routes-and-pages) composition and rendering the
whole tree as a navigable site. The same machinery serves any docs-shaped workbook,
including yours.

## What the runtime renders

You declare structure — sections and pages — and the platform's site mode does the
rest:

- a **sidebar** built from your `section` / `page` declarations,
- clean, history-routed **URLs** (`/section/page`), reload-safe so a deep link works,
- server-rendered **prose** for each page, with internal links via `[text](/section/page)`,
- an interactive **examples** explorer and a **blog**, when you include them.

The look is yours — it comes from a brand sheet in your composition root, never from
the runtime. The [Nexus](/introduction/what-is-the-nexus) ships unopinionated
plumbing; you supply the title and the theme.

## Built to be read by agents

A docs site is also a corpus an agent should be able to ingest whole. Site mode emits
machine-readable surfaces alongside the human pages:

- **`/llms.txt`** — a compact, machine-readable index of the site: the map.
- **`/llms-full.txt`** — a full-text dump of every page: the whole book in one fetch.

Point an agent at `llms.txt` for the structure, feed it `llms-full.txt` for the
content. Each page also offers **copy-as-markdown** and **copy-as-prompt**, so a
single page drops straight into a chat. The docs are agent-ready by construction —
see [Get started with your CLI agent](/tooling/get-started-with-your-cli-agent).

## Why render it server-side

Server-rendering the prose means the site is fast, linkable, and indexable without
shipping a front-end framework to do routing. The [`client`](/language/placement-and-languages)
islands that *do* need to be interactive (the examples explorer) hydrate as wasm in
the page; everything else is just rendered HTML. You get a real site without writing
one.

## The same shape, scaled

Whether the runtime serves this one docs workbook or a dozen apps side by side, site
mode is the same — [one nexus, many sites](/blog/the-nexus-serves-many-sites), each a
tree the runtime renders. Declare the structure; the site follows.
